 to shape messages that move people and change the world.Every Communications Program course assumes a fluency with the English language. Attendance at first class required.","ever_bidding":true,"faculty_category":null,"faculty_title":null,"has_bidding":true,"has_eval":false,"id":"DPI-835-M||2025||Fall||Krupin, Stephen","instructor_label":"No Data","is_average":false,"is_core":false,"is_stem":false,"last_bid_acad":"2025-2026","last_bid_capacity":18,"last_bid_n_bids":33,"last_bid_price":978.0,"last_bid_term":"Spring","location":null,"meeting_days":null,"metrics_pct":{"Assignments":null,"Availability":null,"Bid_N_Bids":null,"Bid_Price":null,"Course_Rating":null,"Discussion Diversity":null,"Discussions":null,"Diverse Perspectives":null,"Feedback":null,"Insights":null,"Instructor_Rating":null,"Readings":null,"Rigor":null,"Workload":null},"metrics_raw":{"Assignments":null,"Availability":null,"Bid_N_Bids":null,"Bid_Price":759.0,"Course_Rating":null,"Discussion Diversity":null,"Discussions":null,"Diverse Perspectives":null,"Feedback":null,"Insights":null,"Instructor_Rating":null,"Readings":null,"Rigor":null,"Workload":null},"n_respondents":null,"n_terms":1,"professor":"Krupin, Stephen","professor_display":"Stephen Krupin","stem_group":null,"stem_school":null,"term":"Fall","time_end":null,"time_start":null,"total_n_respondents":null,"workload_label":"No Data","year":2025,"year_range":null},{"bid_academic_year":"2025-2026","bid_capacity":18,"bid_clearing_price":978.0,"bid_n_bids":33,"concentration":"DPI","course_code":"DPI-835-M","course_code_base":"DPI-835-M","course_name":"Speechwriting","course_url":"https://www.hks.harvard.edu/courses/speechwriting","description":"What makes a speech persuasive and memorable – and how do you write one? How can storytelling help political, corporate, nonprofit, and community leaders achieve their goals? What is the role of the speech in our politics, policymaking, and international relations? This course will explore the techniques speechwriters and speakers use, from research to rhetoric, to shape messages that move people and change the world.Every Communications Program course assumes a fluency with the English language. Attendance at first class required.","ever_bidding":true,"faculty_category":null,"faculty_title":null,"has_bidding":true,"has_eval":false,"id":"DPI-835-M||2026||Spring||Krupin, Stephen","instructor_label":"No Data","is_average":false,"is_core":false,"is_stem":false,"last_bid_acad":"2025-2026","last_bid_capacity":18,"last_bid_n_bids":33,"last_bid_price":978.0,"last_bid_term":"Spring","location":null,"meeting_days":null,"metrics_pct":{"Assignments":null,"Availability":null,"Bid_N_Bids":null,"Bid_Price":null,"Course_Rating":null,"Discussion Diversity":null,"Discussions":null,"Diverse Perspectives":null,"Feedback":null,"Insights":null,"Instructor_Rating":null,"Readings":null,"Rigor":null,"Workload":null},"metrics_raw":{"Assignments":null,"Availability":null,"Bid_N_Bids":33.0,"Bid_Price":978.0,"Course_Rating":null,"Discussion Diversity":null,"Discussions":null,"Diverse Perspectives":null,"Feedback":null,"Insights":null,"Instructor_Rating":null,"Readings":null,"Rigor":null,"Workload":null},"n_respondents":null,"n_terms":1,"professor":"Krupin, Stephen","professor_display":"Stephen Krupin","stem_group":null,"stem_school":null,"term":"Spring","time_end":null,"time_start":null,"total_n_respondents":null,"workload_label":"No Data","year":2026,"year_range":null},{"bid_academic_year":"2025-2026","bid_capacity":null,"bid_clearing_price":1.0,"bid_n_bids":null,"concentration":"DPI","course_code":"DPI-840-M","course_code_base":"DPI-840-M","course_name":"Advanced Intensive Writing: Analytical Writing for Policy Journals and Other Publications","course_url":"https://www.hks.harvard.edu/courses/feature-writing","description":"This intensive module provides a thorough grounding in the techniques of journalistic feature writing: researching, reporting, interviewing, writing — and revising. We investigate where good feature ideas come from; we explore how to conceptualize, organize, and structure those ideas through journalistic narrative; and we experiment in a collaborative workshop environment with several journalistic forms — the profile, the reported essay, the “issue” story, the “trend” piece. Students will gain proficiency in the techniques of journalistic feature writing, skills that are relevant to other forms of nonfiction storytelling, too, including academic and policy writing.Every Communications Program course assumes a fluency with the English language. Attendance at first class required.","ever_bidding":true,"faculty_category":null,"faculty_title":null,"has_bidding":true,"has_eval":false,"id":"DPI-840-M||2025||Fall||Geary, James","instructor_label":"No Data","is_average":false,"is_core":false,"is_stem":false,"last_bid_acad":"2025-2026","last_bid_capacity":null,"last_bid_n_bids":null,"last_bid_price":1.0,"last_bid_term":"Fall","location":null,"meeting_days":null,"metrics_pct":{"Assignments":null,"Availability":null,"Bid_N_Bids":null,"Bid_Price":null,"Course_Rating":null,"Discussion Diversity":null,"Discussions":null,"Diverse Perspectives":null,"Feedback":null,"Insights":null,"Instructor_Rating":null,"Readings":null,"Rigor":null,"Workload":null},"metrics_raw":{"Assignments":null,"Availability":null,"Bid_N_Bids":null,"Bid_Price":1.0,"Course_Rating":null,"Discussion Diversity":null,"Discussions":null,"Diverse Perspectives":null,"Feedback":null,"Insights":null,"Instructor_Rating":null,"Readings":null,"Rigor":null,"Workload":null},"n_respondents":null,"n_terms":1,"professor":"Geary, James","professor_display":"James Geary","stem_group":null,"stem_school":null,"term":"Fall","time_end":null,"time_start":null,"total_n_respondents":null,"workload_label":"No Data","year":2025,"year_range":null},{"bid_academic_year":null,"bid_capacity":null,"bid_clearing_price":null,"bid_n_bids":null,"concentration":"IGA","course_code":"IGA-229","course_code_base":"IGA-229","course_name":"Gender, Sex, and Violence in Global Politics","course_url":"https://www.hks.harvard.edu/courses/sex-and-violence-global-politics","description":"In this course, we will consider the international and global dimensions of gender, sex and violence, both within and outside the context of armed conflict. Current policy debates are informed by powerful—and often unquestioned—assumptions about sex, gender and violence. Recent research has challenged some of these ideas, and policymakers have responded with calls for better data, increased attention to long-hidden problems, and new strategies to confront these difficult challenges. In the course, we will consider a series of policy-relevant questions on the politics of sex, gender, and violence. Topics that we will cover include the sexed and gendered causes and consequences of war (e.g., Do sex and gender inequalities cause armed conflict? Are women leaders more peaceful? What are the consequences of women serving in frontline combat roles? ); gendered motivations for political violence (e.g., What drives people to choose violence?); the regulation of sex and gender within state and non-state armed groups, including militaries, insurgencies and terrorist organizations; the causes and consequences of wartime sexual violence; and the global politics of abortion, sex work and human trafficking. The course will feature a multi-media case, guest speakers, including policymakers, practitioners and academic researchers , and will include discussions of research design and implementation, as well as policy responses and interventions.","ever_bidding":false,"faculty_category":null,"faculty_title":null,"has_bidding":false,"has_eval":true,"id":"IGA-229||0||Average||Cohen, Dara Kay||aggregate-d3fefba52341","instructor_label":"Outstanding","is_average":true,"is_core":false,"is_stem":false,"last_bid_acad":null,"last_bid_capacity":null,"last_bid_n_bids":null,"last_bid_price":null,"last_bid_term":null,"location":null,"meeti